{name:'Bartolomé Hidalgo',period:'1821–1822',work:'Diálogos patrióticos',argument:'Hidalgo helped establish the gauchesque dialogue as a literary form in which rural speakers debate public life. These are authored texts, not verbatim recordings of laborers.',question:'How does dialogue change the power of a rural literary voice?',source:'https://www.cervantesvirtual.com/obra-visor/dialogos--1/html/ff9c0bfc-82b1-11df-acc7-002185ce6064_2.html',sourceLabel:'Biblioteca Virtual Miguel de Cervantes · Diálogos'},
{name:'Hilario Ascasubi',period:'nineteenth century',work:'Santos Vega o Los mellizos de la Flor',argument:'Ascasubi shows that gauchesque literature includes competing social perspectives and poetic forms. Hernández belongs to a tradition, not an isolated invention of the gaucho voice.',question:'Where do Ascasubi and Hernández differ in narrative outlook?',source:'https://www.cervantesvirtual.com/portales/literatura_gauchesca/introduccion/',sourceLabel:'Cervantes Virtual · gauchesque literature'},
{name:'Lucio V. Mansilla',period:'1870',work:'Una excursión a los indios ranqueles',argument:'Mansilla’s frontier travel narrative records encounters and negotiations with Ranquel leaders, while remaining filtered through his own position as a military officer and writer. It is a useful comparison—not an Indigenous-authored account.',question:'What aspects of diplomacy complicate a frontier narrative dominated by conflict?',source:'https://library.si.edu/digital-library/book/unaexcursinlosin01mans',sourceLabel:'Smithsonian Libraries · historical volume'},
{name:'Leopoldo Lugones',period:'1913 lectures; 1916 book',work:'El payador',argument:'Lugones advanced a highly influential account of Martín Fierro as a national epic. That interpretation is part of the poem’s historical reception and should not be mistaken for an uncontested label supplied by Hernández.',question:'Who decides that one literary work speaks for a nation?',source:'https://fierro.bn.gov.ar/micrositios/libros/literatura/el-payador',sourceLabel:'Biblioteca Nacional · El payador'},
{name:'Ezequiel Martínez Estrada',period:'1948',work:'Muerte y transfiguración de Martín Fierro',argument:'Martínez Estrada’s major reassessment examines conflicts and darker features of Argentine society rather than offering an uncomplicated patriotic celebration. His book is cited and discussed, not reproduced.',question:'What is gained by reading a national literary icon against the grain?',source:'https://www.bn.gov.ar/noticias/14-de-septiembre-de-1895-nace-ezequiel-martinez-estrada',sourceLabel:'Biblioteca Nacional · author and context'},
