<Base lang="en-US" pageType="CollectionPage" title="Critical Library — Martín Fierro and Its Literary Interpreters" description="English scholarly orientation to Hidalgo, Ascasubi, Mansilla, Lugones, Martínez Estrada and Borges, their works and the critical reception of Martín Fierro.">
<article class="critical"><nav><a href="/en/">English edition</a> / <a href="/en/library/">Popular library</a> / Critical library</nav><p class="eyebrow">DOCUMENTARY LIBRARY · LITERARY CONTEXT</p><h1>The critical library: six writers who illuminate Martín Fierro</h1><p class="lead">José Hernández’s poem stands within a literary tradition and a history of vigorous disagreement. Meet six writers who anticipated, contextualized or reinterpreted its questions.</p><p class="notice"><strong>Method:</strong> These original English summaries are introductory interpretation, not direct quotations from the named works. Historical publications and later criticism must be distinguished from the poem. Protected works are not reproduced.</p>
